It does NOT cover the corpus text in shards/, nor the frequency tables in
results/ that are derived from it. That text is not MonDevHub's to license
under MIT: the largest source is Mon Wikipedia, which is CC BY-SA 4.0 and
therefore copyleft, and at least one source has no established licence at all.
An MIT grant over that material would strip a ShareAlike obligation this
project cannot waive and issue a permission this project does not hold.

For the corpus, see LICENSE-CORPUS.md. It states the terms per source, keyed
to the shard filename prefix, and names the sources whose terms are unresolved.

